/T (A: On the western side of the Keystone glows the Great Hercules Cluster. B: Between the bright stars Antares and Altair, hides an area containing many star clusters and nebulae. C: 40% of the way between Altair and Vega, twinkles the "Coathanger," a group of stars outlining a coathanger. D: Sweep along the Milky Way for an astounding number of faint glows and dark bays, including the Great Rift. E: The three westernmost stars of Cassiopeia's "W" point south to M31, the Andromeda Galaxy, a "fuzzy" oval.)
/E (A: On the western side of the Keystone glows the Great Hercules Cluster. B: Between the bright stars Antares and Altair, hides an area containing many star clusters and nebulae. C: 40% of the way between Altair and Vega, twinkles the "Coathanger," a group of stars outlining a coathanger. D: Sweep along the Milky Way for an astounding number of faint glows and dark bays, including the Great Rift. E: The three westernmost stars of Cassiopeia's "W" point south to M31, the Andromeda Galaxy, a "fuzzy" oval.)
